<title>UK: UK to propose treaty changes to IGC Tuesday.</title>
<headline>UK to propose treaty changes to IGC Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's ambassador to the European Union will on Tuesday present proposals to change EU laws after the European Court of Justice ruled Britain must obey a law setting a maximum enforced working week of 48 hours.</p>
<p>A British official said the ambassador would make the proposals to the representatives group of the inter-governmental conference (IGC).</p>
<p>The official said the ambassador would present a protocol to exclude Britain from the working week law and would also press for changes to the current EU treaty so that social policy matters were not decided by majority voting.</p>
</text>
